From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:30:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 71/72] gtk: hotty layers are GL textures over the terminal's

RenderSurface snapshots each hotty layer as its own texture over the
terminal's, where the frame says it shows, clipped to its placement. A
layer's texture is one of up to three GL textures in a context shared
with GTK's: the next is brought up to date from the newest on the GPU
(glCopyImageSubData), and only the rectangles that changed are uploaded
(glTexSubImage2D), behind a fence GTK waits on. GTK 4.24 uploads a memory
texture whole even with an update region, so it is used only without GL.
---
